  "0_outline_root": "ROOT: Column Handling > Requirements",
  "0_outline_lines": [
    "L034: \"All columns defined by FOCUS MUST follow the following rules:\"",
    "  L035: \"Column IDs MUST use [Pascal case](#glossary:pascalcase).\"",
    "  L036: \"Column IDs MUST NOT use abbreviations.\"",
    "  L037: \"Column IDs MUST be alphanumeric with no special characters.\"",
    "  L038: \"Column IDs SHOULD NOT use acronyms.\"",
    "  L039: \"Column IDs SHOULD NOT exceed 50 characters to accommodate column length restrictions of various data repositories.\"",
    "  L040: \"Columns that have an ID and a Name MUST have the `Id` or `Name` suffix in the Column ID.\"",
    "  L041: \"Column display names MUST be consistent with their Column IDs, with spaces inserted between words (e.g., Column ID \\\"BillingAccountName\\\" and display name \\\"Billing Account Name\\\").\"",
    "  L042: \"Columns with the `Category` suffix MUST be normalized.\"",
    "L043: \"<a name=\\\"column_handling:custom-column\\\"></a>Custom (e.g., service-provider-defined) columns that are not defined by FOCUS but included in a *FOCUS dataset* MUST follow the following rules:\"",
    "  L044: \"Custom columns MUST be prefixed with a consistent `x_` prefix to identify them as external, custom columns and distinguish them from FOCUS columns to avoid conflicts in future releases.\"",
    "  L045: \"Custom columns SHOULD follow the same rules listed above for FOCUS columns.\"",
    "  L046: \"Custom columns MUST be detailed in publicly-available documentation, including description, purpose, and relationship to [*native dataset*](#glossary:native-dataset) columns.\""
  ],
